	<item>
		<title>FCC green lights SpaceX’s plan to launch 1 million ‘Starmind&#8217; data center satellites</title>
		<link>https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/11/26/fcc-green-lights-spacexs-plan-to-launch-1-million-starmind-data-center-satellites/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Will Robinson-Smith]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:27:58 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[FCC]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[SpaceX]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Starmind]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Starship]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://spaceflightnow.com/?p=75025</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[The authorization granted by the Federal Communications Commission requires SpaceX to deploy the first of these satellites by Nov. 25, 2033. The full constellation is required to be operational no later than Nov. 25, 2040. <a class="mh-excerpt-more" href="https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/11/26/fcc-green-lights-spacexs-plan-to-launch-1-million-starmind-data-center-satellites/" title="FCC green lights SpaceX’s plan to launch 1 million ‘Starmind&#8217; data center satellites"></a>]]></description>
										
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>SpaceX launches classified payload for the U.S. Space Force</title>
		<link>https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/11/23/live-coverage-spacex-to-launch-classified-payload-for-the-u-s-space-force-3/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Will Robinson-Smith]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:21:32 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Falcon 9]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Mission Reports]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[B1081]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[SLC-4E]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[SLD 30]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[SpaceX]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[U.S. Space Force]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[USSF-266]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://spaceflightnow.com/?p=75012</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[The mission is the third in a series of flights for the U.S. Space Force with a ‘TH’ designation in public filings. Liftoff from pad 4E at Vandenberg Space Force Base is scheduled during a window that opens at 7:55 a.m. PST (10:55 a.m. EST / 1555 UTC). <a class="mh-excerpt-more" href="https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/11/23/live-coverage-spacex-to-launch-classified-payload-for-the-u-s-space-force-3/" title="SpaceX launches classified payload for the U.S. Space Force"></a>]]></description>
										
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Arianespace launches 36 Amazon Leo sats amid rocket crunch</title>
		<link>https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/11/23/live-coverage-arianespaces-launches-amazon-leo-sats-amid-rocket-crunch/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Will Robinson-Smith]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:14:49 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Ariane 6]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Mission Reports]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Amazon Leo]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ariane 64]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Arianespace]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[LE-04]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Leo Europe 4]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://spaceflightnow.com/?p=75000</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[The Leo Europe 4 mission is the fourth flight of Amazon Leo satellites on an Ariane 6 rocket and the 16th launch for the constellation. Liftoff from Europe’s Spaceport in French Guiana happened at 8:14 a.m. Kourou Time (6:14 a.m. EST / 1114 UTC) at the end of the launch window. <a class="mh-excerpt-more" href="https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/11/23/live-coverage-arianespaces-launches-amazon-leo-sats-amid-rocket-crunch/" title="Arianespace launches 36 Amazon Leo sats amid rocket crunch"></a>]]></description>
										
					
		
		
			</item>
